 (United States)","location":"Dallas, Texas, United States"}},"id":"a1a23e580c114acabf98e4db08b39ee5","userType":"CONTRACTOR_GRANTEE","userId":"505134e1b3de416fa3d28f1ecd3084ff"}],"stiTypeDetails":"Technical Publication (TP)","technicalReviewType":"SINGLE_EXPERT","modified":"2025-08-31T18:39:21.7150190+00:00","id":20210024855,"created":"2021-11-23T19:34:11.3566990+00:00","center":{"code":"JSC","name":"Johnson Space Center","id":"dd46994b91a94cb2a2722617cbbadc55"},"onlyAbstract":false,"sensitiveInformation":2,"abstract":"The Life Support Baseline Values and Assumptions Document (BVAD) provides analysts, modelers, and other life support researchers with a common set of values and assumptions which can be used as a baseline in their studies.  This baseline, in turn, provides a common point of origin from which many studies in the community may depart, making research results easier to compare and providing researchers with reasonable values to assume for areas outside their experience. With the ability to accurately compare different technologies’ performance for the same function, managers will be able to make better decisions regarding technology development.","isLessonsLearned":true,"disseminated":"DOCUMENT_AND_METADATA","cui":{"isCui":false,"submissionId":20210024855,"id":"1b5053a6b6de4cfe9dd1fb07f314e0eb"},"publications":[{"submissionId":20210024855,"publisher":"","id":"a6ce3b53c68e47299b2ea7cd5f5327ff","publicationName":"","publicationDate":"2022-02-01T05:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[],"downloads":[{"draft":false,"mimetype":"application/pdf","name":"BVAD_2.15.22-final.pdf","type":"STI","links":{"original":"/api/citations/20210024855/downloads/BVAD_2.15.22-final.pdf","pdf":"/api/citations/20210024855/downloads/BVAD_2.15.22-final.pdf","fulltext":"/api/citations/20210024855/downloads/BVAD_2.15.22-final.pdf.txt"}}],"downloadsAvailable":true,"index":"submissions-2026-11-05-06-21"}